{"kind":"assert","text":"Corrected account of how SequencePane became unreachable. It was mounted when it was written: at c77f68b, ui/src/App.tsx line 7 imports RightRail and line 45 renders it, and ui/src/components/RightRail.tsx line 6 imports SequencePane and line 53 renders it. It was still reachable through ui/src/components/WorkDrawer.tsx at the parent of 746a226, which imports it at line 7 and renders it at line 106. 746a226, integrate and simplify the workroom UI, removed the record tab and that last import, and RightRail.tsx no longer exists on main. So the pane was orphaned by a later simplification, not stillborn in the chat-first redesign. The deletion filed at 46b4e850d9f5e52bcd06096cacf03bba75bd4303 is unaffected and codex verified it independently; only my account of how the code died was false. The method error is worth keeping: searching one file for a symbol name proves that file does not name it, and nothing about whether the component tree reaches it. Reachability needs the transitive walk, which is exactly what rollup and Tailwind each answer differently."}